From cbcaa8343590f3aa59db36f23e17f2957f0069c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:41:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] libcpp: Fix up parsing __has_include outside directive
 [PR121508]

The r17-4537 change broke several tests especially by introducing
non-determinism into the preprocessor.  The builtin_has_include_1
function is expected to set *paren and *bracket flags, and early
exit from the function without setting those flags means the callers
then use uninitialized variables.  Also, the early exit means that
when (incorrectly, sure) one uses __has_include/__has_include_next
or __has_embed outside of a preprocessing directive but with
correct syntax, it is diagnosed as both using it outside of
a preprocessing directive (correct) but also as a random sequence
of unexpected tokens.  This patch reverts that change.

I'm guilty of introducing _cpp_get_token_no_padding 6 years ago
instead of fixing up get_token_no_padding back then, I wasn't
sure if the eating of CPP_EOF wasn't intentional in some cases,
but clearly it is never intentional and always a bug.
After all, get__Pragma_string has been fighting with it already
by using
  paren = get_token_no_padding (pfile);
  if (paren->type == CPP_EOF)
    _cpp_backup_tokens (pfile, 1);
glue_header_name and parse_include weren't doing this, but in
the usual case when pfile->state.in_directive and not lexing a raw string,
get_fresh_line_impl returns false and _cpp_lex_direct will just keep
returning CPP_EOF at the end of the line many times until we clear
the pfile->state.in_directive flag.
So, I think we should just drop the dangerous get_token_no_padding
function and simply never eat a CPP_EOF.

2026-10-09  Jakub Jelinek  <jakub@redhat.com>

	PR preprocessor/121508
	PR preprocessor/123339
	* directives.cc (get_token_no_padding): Remove.
	(glue_header_name): Use _cpp_get_token_no_padding instead of
	get_token_no_padding.
	(parse_include): Likewise.
	(get__Pragma_string): Likewise.  Don't _cpp_backup_tokens on
	CPP_EOF.

	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr121508-1.c: New test.
	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr121508-2.c: New test.
	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr121508-3.c: New test.
	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr121508-4.c: New test.
	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr121508-5.c: New test.
	* c-c++-common/cpp/pr123339.c: New test.

Reviewed-by: Andrea Pinski <andrew.pinski@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9e5fda8ec5716b6fa2b57bdfd56e2b91116a93ff)
